   "he": "אוֹנֵן פָּסוּל. אָמַר רָבָא: לֹא שָׁנוּ אֶלָּא בְּקׇרְבַּן יָחִיד, אֲבָל בְּקׇרְבַּן צִבּוּר – מְרַצֶּה, קַל וָחוֹמֶר מִטּוּמְאָה;",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that if «an acute mourner» collects the blood of an offering, the offering is «disqualified. Rava says: They taught» this «only with regard to an individual’s offering. But with regard to a communal offering,» a rite performed by an acute mourner does «effect acceptance.» One can derive this by «a fortiori» inference «from ritual impurity.»"
  }
